  "description": "A fast breakdown of Critical Periods for builders.",
  "is_free": false,
  "published": true,
  "story": {
    "hook": {
      "text": "Cover one eye of a kitten for a few weeks during early life and it will never develop normal vision in that eye.",
      "visual": "🐱"
    },
    "buildup": {
      "text": "Critical periods are time windows in early development when the brain is extraordinarily sensitive to specific experiences.",
      "visual": "⏰"
    },
    "discovery": {
      "text": "Without the right input, wiring goes wrong permanently.",
      "visual": "🔌"
    },
    "twist": {
      "text": "Language has a critical period too.",
      "visual": "🗣️"
    },
    "climax": {
      "text": "Critical periods close when molecular brakes, like perineuronal nets, lock circuits in place to stabilize what the brain has.",
      "visual": "🔒"
    },
    "punchline": {
      "text": "The young brain trades flexibility for stability.",
      "visual": "🧱"
    }
  },
  "quiz": {
    "question": "What are critical periods?",
    "options": [
      "Time windows when the brain is highly sensitive to specific experiences",
      "Moments when the brain stops growing entirely",
      "Periods when neurons divide rapidly"
    ],
    "correct": 0
  },
